A||N||13||FieroKyle||SAD DAY!!! Fiero hit a tree!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||08-06-2001||07:18 PM||||I was packing my car till 2 AM for a camping trip and went to bed to wake up my car rolled down the hill into a tree..... Since of the limited space i was shoving clothes and stuff behind the seats when I think I knocked it out of gear. (manual tranny). And the E-brake doesn't work =(. Luckily I have the car fully covered in insurance ($100 deductable in comprehensive) and with repairs it should be back on the road soon. I took it to the body shop for an estimate (Elite Auto Body for Lowell or Grand Rapids area Fiero owners). $1700 so the car isn't totaled. The car runs great and everything is supposed to be like it is except for the left blinker not working. It rolled about 50 feet till it hit on relativily flat pavement. So the fiero is once again out of commission until further notice. This is a warning too for stick shift owners make sure the car is in 1st gear, =). Later peeps. I will keep ya all updated on the Fiero trauma.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg">  <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>AOL Name: Yakty Yak<BR>E-Mail: YaktyYak@aol.com<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||sloth85GT||08-06-2001||07:32 PM||||ahhhhhh that's why you gotta love the prairies. Winnipeg is as flat as it gets so I have no worries about that. But I feel your pain dude. Sorry to hear that such a sweet car got banged up. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif"> <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
