Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||08-07-2001||11:04 AM||||it rolled 50 feet on relatively flat pavement and did $1700 damage to itself?!<P> WOW! thats scary!<P>  not to make light of your loss, but you should of been a soap box derby racer when you were a kid - 50 feet is only like 3 car lengths.<P> BTW I put my Ebrake on tight everytime I park, and it wont hold the car on level ground either - someday Ill figure out why.||||reg||11
Z||000006||FieroKyle||08-07-2001||12:32 PM||||Fiero Update, DAY 2: Took it into the insurance company so they could look at the damage. Their estimate was only $998. So I think they are trying to give me the royal screw job on how the car should be fixed and the cheapest it can be fixed without being too noticable.||||reg||8
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||12:43 PM||||when you take it to a shop, if its more than insurance estimate they can add what are called 'supplements' to raise it high enough to cover damage. I do it all the time, sometimes almost doubling the original estimate. Just dont sign over any checks till your satisfied. When you sign it in most places thats like your approval on the repairs. I did a brand new Firebird that was hit really hard and added over $9,000 in supplements over the orig est.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroKyle||08-07-2001||01:02 PM||||Well at this body shop, I know most of the guys there. They won't screw me over, just worried State Farm might. I also trying to have them fix a cracked rocker panel from a flat tire while they are at it and add it to the insurance.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Capt Fiero||08-07-2001||01:12 PM||||I cant say about how your auto ins is done but here in BC "ALL" of our auto ins is ran by the provincial goverment.  And when I had a front end accident they told me there was 3000+ in damage, and they wanted to write the car off, I more or less told them where they could stick that idea. They agreed to (with some arguing) to cut me a check for 2500$ and give me the car back with a clean title. NO REBUILD ON IT. As I told them that the car was not a right off, it was simply due to there cost in parts that it was going to be written off and I told them I would cover the balance of repairing the car if they would just pay me instead of a shop. They agreed and cut me a cheque for $2550. Now for the funny part.  Their quotes<BR>Hood 450$<BR>2 Fenders 400$<BR>Nose Cone 600$<BR>and the list went on and on.<BR>I called the local kit car guy and said I need some stock black 85 Fiero body panels as well as the front rebar and such plus other bits and pieces.  <P>I walked away with a pick up load of everything that i needed for 350$ spent a weekend ripping the front of the car apart and replacing a ton of parts and the car is back on the road today. I used the extra money for my alarm+keyless entry, GA brake conversion, and part of it for my engine build up.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||sloth85GT||08-07-2001||01:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baldlobo:<BR>[B]winnipeg is not flat sloth, saskatoon, or regina is flat. And sorry to hear about your car.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe  not where you live, but I never really have to use my parking brake or put my car in gear when parking (I do though anyway cause that'd be stupid if I didn't). Compared to the east coast, or vancouver, yes, it's flat. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif"> <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||10
